func instrumentContext(ctx context.Context, endpoint string, pCtx backend.PluginContext) context.Context {
	p := []any{"endpoint", endpoint, "pluginId", pCtx.PluginID}   // allocation on every call
	if pCtx.DataSourceInstanceSettings != nil { p = append(p, "dsName", ..., "dsUID", ...) }
	if pCtx.User != nil { p = append(p, "uname", pCtx.User.Login) }
	return log.WithContextualAttributes(ctx, p)   // context.WithValue on every call
}
func (m *ContextualLoggerMiddleware) QueryData(ctx context.Context, req *backend.QueryDataRequest) (*backend.QueryDataResponse, error) {
	ctx = instrumentContext(ctx, endpointQueryData, req.PluginContext)   // always called
	return m.next.QueryData(ctx, req)
}
```

Contrast — pkg/services/pluginsintegration/clientmiddleware/logger_middleware.go:18-28:
```go
func NewLoggerMiddleware(cfg *setting.Cfg, logger plog.Logger) plugins.ClientMiddleware {
	return plugins.ClientMiddlewareFunc(func(next plugins.Client) plugins.Client {
		if !cfg.PluginLogBackendRequests {   // line 20 — gated; pass-through when logging disabled
			return next
		}
		return &LoggerMiddleware{next: next, logger: logger}
	})
}
```

findings.suggestion:
Gate ContextualLoggerMiddleware the same way LoggerMiddleware is, so the contextual-attr injection only happens when plugin request instrumentation is actually enabled:

```go
func NewContextualLoggerMiddleware(cfg *setting.Cfg) plugins.ClientMiddleware {
    return plugins.ClientMiddlewareFunc(func(next plugins.Client) plugins.Client {
        if !cfg.PluginLogBackendRequests {
            return next
        }
        return &ContextualLoggerMiddleware{next: next}
    })
}
```
and update the call site (pluginsintegration.go:160) to `clientmiddleware.NewContextualLoggerMiddleware(cfg)`. If the contextual attributes are intentionally required by downstream middlewares (e.g. the tracing or metrics middleware reading them via log.FromContext) regardless of the log-backend-requests flag, add a comment at the call site documenting that justification and consider a cheaper injection path (e.g. reusing a pooled []any, or only attaching the pluginId scalar) when logging is disabled.
